<title>HONG KONG: Nintendo in action against HK retailers.</title>
<headline>Nintendo in action against HK retailers.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nintendo Co Ltd, which develops and markets &quot;Gameboy&quot; hand-held game consoles and cartridges, said on Monday it has issued writs to 17 Hong Kong retail shops alleged to have sold counterfeit Gameboy game cartridges.</p>
<p>Hong Kong customs, with cooperation from Nintendo, recently raided five retailers in which HK$1.5 million worth of Nintendo software was confiscated, Nintendo said in a statement.</p>
<p>Nintendo owns the copyright and industrial design of its games, and the company's trademarks under which its products are sold worldwide.</p>
<p>In 1996, local customs seized more than 3,000 counterfeit copies of Nintendo software, resulting in over 40 criminal actions by the government, the statement said.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6590</p>
